ASSESSMENT

Irritable Bowel Syndrome with functional abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting.

PLAN

Ms. Edwards is a pleasant 32-year-old female who was last seen in August 2019 with flares of abdominal pain, who was diagnosed with irritable bowel syndrome. She has had a previous prescription for Reglan that she received from the emergency room that she used as needed for nausea. She was instructed to start a low dose fiber supplement, such as Citrucel, daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, Bentyl up to 4 times daily for intestinal cramping, and stop Reglan and use Zofran as needed. Neuromodulators such as Elavil and Buspar were discussed but not started.

The patient reports she is a pleasant 32-year-old female who was last seen in August 2019 with flares of abdominal pain, who was diagnosed with irritable bowel syndrome. She has had a previous prescription for Reglan that she received from the emergency room that she used as needed for nausea. She was instructed to start a low dose fiber supplement, such as Citrucel, daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, Bentyl up to 4 times daily for intestinal cramping, and stop Reglan and use Zofran as needed. Neuromodulators such as Elavil and Buspar were discussed but not started. She states she has been going out to eat on Friday nights and Saturday nights and that she has had some spicy foods or spicy shrimp. She states she has been getting both lower belly stuff like cramps, or upper belly stuff like nausea. She states she has been having bowel movements 2-3 times a day. She states they are formed. She states after she has gone out drinking with her friends, she tends to have more diarrhea. She states she feels it is the food and the alcohol. She states she usually eats pasta at Friday's restaurant. She states she always eats pasta, chicken alfredo. She states it normally does not bother her. She states she has had some fried chicken today. She states she feels fine. She states she has been avoiding heavy foods. She states she has noticed it is between 2-3 times a day. She states she is still having cramping and sharp pains, so she has been avoiding heavy foods. She states she did have some fried chicken today, though. She states it was all right.

I have encouraged dietary and lifestyle modifications, as well as starting a neuromodulator such as Elavil 25mg at bedtime for irritable bowel syndrome. She can use Bentyl 20mg as needed 30-45 minutes prior to eating out at a restaurant. She can also use Zofran if needed. However, I have encouraged her to reduce greasy and fatty foods and alcohol consumption. I have asked her to follow up in one month by emailing over MyChart regarding any side effects and issues, or issues with Elavil or if adjustments are needed. }}<|eot_id|>
