summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Back pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Noah Brown is a pleasant 55-year-old male who presents today for the evaluation of back pain. He states that his pain began approximately 1 week ago and has been ongoing since then. The pain is located in the middle of his back, which radiates to the left lower back and occasionally to his left eye. He denies any recent injury, but states that the pain is worse with sudden twisting movements to the left. The patient reports that he has tried over-the-counter medications and has been taking ibuprofen 4 times a day, but his pain is not improving. He denies any numbness, tingling, or weakness in his legs. The patient has a history of diabetes and has been doing well with his current regimen of metformin 2 times a day.

The patient also reports that he has been trying to exercise and diet well. He states that he has been eating sugar, but does not have a regular diet. He denies any recent weight loss.

The patient also has a family history of diabetes.

MEDICATIONS

Metformin 2 times a day.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Reports a recent weight loss, but denies fever, chills, or night sweats.
• Musculoskeletal: Reports back pain.
• Neurological: Denies numbness, tingling, or weakness in the legs.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• General: Alert and in no apparent distress.
• Respiratory: Auscultation of the lungs reveals clear bilaterally.
• Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm.
• Musculoskeletal: Examination of the back reveals pain to palpation in the mid-back, worse on the left. The patient has pain on extension and rotation to the left. There is no pain on straight leg raising bilaterally.

RESULTS

X-ray of the lumbar spine was ordered.

ASSESSMENT

• Back pain.
• Diabetes.

PLAN

The patient will undergo a low back x-ray as an outpatient. I will order physical therapy to help with pain and strengthen his back muscles. I will also prescribe Flexeril 10 mg once a day. The patient will continue to take ibuprofen 400 mg every 4-6 hours as needed. He will continue his current regimen of metformin 2 times a day. The patient will also continue to monitor his blood sugar levels and will follow up with me in 1 month for a follow-up appointment. I will also order a hemoglobin A1c at this time.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will continue to monitor his blood sugar levels. He will continue to take ibuprofen 400 mg every 4-6 hours as needed. The patient will continue his current regimen of metformin 2 times a day. He will follow up with me in 1 month for a follow-up appointment. I will also order a hemoglobin A1c at this time.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>
