summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Acute onset chest pain.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports she has been walking her dog every day, approximately 1.5 miles.

MEDICATIONS

• Aspirin 81 mg daily
• Brilinta 90 mg twice daily
• Lipitor 80 mg daily
• Toprol 50 mg daily
• Metformin

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain or shortness of breath. Endorses lower extremity edema.
• Respiratory: Denies dyspnea.
• Musculoskeletal: Endorses right leg swelling.
• Neurological: Denies weakness or numbness in the legs.
• Skin: Denies rash.

VITALS

• Blood pressure: 120/80 mmHg
• Heart rate: 60/min
• Respiratory rate: 18/min
• Oxygen saturation: 98% on room air

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Neck: No jugular venous distension. No carotid bruits.
• Cardiovascular: 3/6 systolic ejection murmur heard at the left base.
• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.
• Musculoskeletal: 1+ pitting edema of the right lower extremity. No calf tenderness.

RESULTS

• ECG: Normal sinus rhythm with a good R wave progression. Evolutionary changes consistent with a recent STEMI.
• Echocardiogram: Reduced ejection fraction of 35%. Moderate mitral regurgitation.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

1. Coronary artery disease.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient presents with a history of coronary artery disease and recent ST elevation myocardial infarction. She is compliant with her medications and is currently on a high-dose statin.
• Medical Treatment: Continue aspirin 81 mg daily, Brilinta 90 mg twice daily, Lipitor 80 mg daily, and Toprol 50 mg daily.
2. Reduced left ventricular dysfunction and moderate mitral regurgitation.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient's recent echocardiogram showed a reduced ejection fraction of 35%. The patient is compliant with her medications and will continue to be monitored.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Lisinopril 20 mg daily.
3. Acute heart failure.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient has recently developed lower extremity edema and is now retaining fluid. She will continue to be monitored.
• Medical Treatment: Prescribe Lasix 40 mg daily and Aldactone 12.5 mg daily. We will repeat another echo in 2 months.
4. Hypertension.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient's blood pressure is stable.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Lisinopril 20 mg daily. Nutrition counseling is recommended to consider diet options such as cutting out meat, especially preserved meat, and finding alternatives.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>
