summary is: {{ History of Present Illness: 
The patient is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history of epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease, who presents with left elbow pain. She is a computer programmer and sits at her desk for long periods of time. She has pain on the tip of her left elbow, which is worse on flexion and extension. She has difficulty opening and closing her left elbow. She has some swelling in the area. She is right-handed. She has no numbness or tingling in her hands. She has some weakness in her left arm, but not too significant. She has no fever or chills.

Past Medical History: 
She has epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease. She has been taking keppra for her epilepsy and has not had any seizures in the past year. She has been taking protonix for her peptic ulcer disease and has been doing well. She has been in therapy for depression and has been doing well.

Social History: 
She is a computer programmer and sits at her desk for long periods of time. She has a lot of stress in her job.

Physical Examination: 
She has erythema and edema on her left elbow. She has pain on flexion and extension. She has a palpable radial pulse. She has some pain on palpation of her olecranon.

Impression: 
She has olecranon bursitis. She has depression and is being treated with lexapro. She has peptic ulcer disease and is being treated with protonix.

Plan: 
She will take meloxicam for her olecranon bursitis. She will continue taking keppra for her epilepsy. She will continue taking protonix for her peptic ulcer disease. She will start taking lexapro for her depression. She will have a follow-up appointment in a couple of weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
