summary is: {{ History of Present Illness:
 Mrs. Lee is a 40-year-old female who presents with a 2-day history of left-sided low back pain after a twisting injury at a birthday party. She was jumping out of a surprise party and twisted her back. She has no radiculopathy or numbness down her legs. She has some stiffness with rotation.

Past Medical History:
She has a history of lumbar fusion at T4.

Physical Examination:
The patient has normal vital signs. She has normal lumbar flexion and extension. She has some stiffness with rotation. There is no evidence of a pinched nerve or radiculopathy.

Impression:
She has a lumbar strain.

Plan:
She will be given a prescription for motrin 800mg three times a day with food. She will use ice and heat alternating on her back. She will continue to walk. If her symptoms do not improve or worsen over the next week, she will be seen in the office. }}<|eot_id|>
