summary is: {{ HPC: 27-year-old female patient with a history of carpal tunnel syndrome, chronic back pain, and depression. PMHx: carpal tunnel release 2 years ago. She has been feeling more pain in her right knee, specifically after swimming. No injury, no trauma. PMHx of chronic back pain, stable. Currently on medication for depression, no issues. She has been swimming regularly and has been feeling more pain in her knee. She has been doing breaststroke with her legs kicking out. 
Imp: chondromalacia patellae. Plan: anti-inflammatory medication, straight leg raising exercises, and avoiding activities that put pressure on her knee. Follow up in 2 weeks if no improvement. 
Imp: stable chronic back pain, no change in depression. Imp: stable carpal tunnel syndrome. 
Plan: no changes. }}<|eot_id|>
