summary is: {{ HPC: 31-year-old female with a past medical history of type 2 diabetes and hypertension presents with abnormal lab findings. She has a positive Lyme titer and presents with symptoms of fatigue, joint pain in her elbows, and body aches. She has also had a rash in the past, which is currently resolving. She has been feeling nauseous and has had difficulty eating. She has been having high blood sugars and has had difficulty controlling her blood sugars. She has been on metformin and lisinopril. She has been taking her medications regularly. She has no other symptoms. 

PMHx: Type 2 diabetes, hypertension, hypothyroidism

DHx: No other medical problems

SHx: Works as a nurse, no sick contacts

Impression: Lyme disease

Plan: Doxycycline 100mg PO bid x 3 weeks, to be rechecked in a week. Also, to have a hemoglobin A1C and to be rechecked in a week. Continue metformin and lisinopril. }}<|eot_id|>
