summary is: {{ History of present illness: The patient is a 20-year-old female who is being seen for a yearly follow-up for asthma, allergic rhinitis and food allergy. She has been switched to Wixela due to insurance changes since the last office visit in April 2020. She uses Zyrtec in the spring, summer and fall for seasonal allergy symptoms which tend to work well. She has a known peanut allergy and tolerates almonds and cashews.

Past medical history: She has asthma, allergic rhinitis and food allergy.

Social history: She is a non-smoker, but has been using vape recently. She is trying to quit. She has not had any urgent care or ER visits for breathing issues in the past year.

Immunizations: Up to date.

Review of systems: She has been doing well with no issues with her asthma.

Physical examination: Her lungs sound clear. Her ears, nose and throat are normal. She has no wheezing or rhonchi.

Impression: Asthma, allergic rhinitis and food allergy.

Plan: Continue to use Wixela as needed. Use Zyrtec as needed in the spring, summer and fall. Continue to avoid peanuts and tree nuts. Consider using alvesco instead of Wixela as needed.

Follow-up: In four months for spirometry and act. }}<|eot_id|>
