summary is: {{ HPC: 31-year-old female with history of type 2 diabetes and asthma, presenting with 1 week history of worsening abdominal pain. 
HPC: Abdominal pain worsened with exercise, nausea and vomiting x3 in the past week, mild tenderness in the epigastrium on examination.
Impression: Acute gastritis, related to increased coffee intake and possibly moderate alcohol consumption.
Plan: Zantac 150mg twice a day for 2 weeks, metformin increased to 1000mg in the morning and 500mg in the evening, review in 4 weeks. 
Imp: Diabetes under control, asthma under control on flovent and albuterol as needed. 
Imp: Review in 4 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
