summary is: {{ HPC: 82-year-old male with a past medical history of hypertension and stage three chronic kidney disease presents to the hospital for follow-up after an acute on chronic CHF exacerbation.
SH: He reports being short of breath and having ankle swelling for a few days prior to admission. He has been having difficulty controlling his blood pressure and has been missing some doses of his medications. He has been eating pizza and chicken wings on the weekends and has been having difficulty adhering to his diet.
PMHx: Hypertension, stage three chronic kidney disease
DHx: None
FHx: None
SHx: Lives alone, smokes a pack a day, has no known allergies
Impression: Congestive heart failure, hypertension
PE: BP 128/72, HR 79, RR 26, O2 sat 99% on room air, lungs clear to auscultation, no jugular venous distension, heart sounds normal, no murmurs, bilateral pedal edema
Imp: Congestive heart failure, hypertension
Plan: Continue bumex 2mg daily, continue cozaar 100mg daily, continue norvasc 5mg daily, order renal artery ultrasound, follow up in three months. }}<|eot_id|>
